REVIEW QUESTIONS\
\
1- You have been asked to identify the right type of cloud service to help the team of developers to provide programming elements such as runtime environments. Which service do you recommend?\
A- PaaS\
B- IaaS\
C- SaaS\
D- DaaS\
\
*A. Platform as a service (PaaS) is probably the right level of service for the developer team. It provides infrastructure, like IaaS, and also supplies needed programming elements. Infrastructure  as a service doesn\'92t provide runtime environments; think of it as hardware. Software as a service provides apps and is too high of a service for what\'92s needed here. There is no current DaaS on the exam objectives.\
\
2- You are setting up a cloud contract with a provider. Your team needs the ability to quickly increase capacity to meet peak demands. What do you request?\
A- Elasticity\
B- Availability\
C- Resource pooling\
D- Metered utilization\
\
*A. The ability to expand services quickly refers to elasticity (or specifically, rapid elasticity). Availability guarantees uptime for services. All cloud services use resource pooling. Metered utilization is how many suppliers track usage and charge accordingly.\
\
3- Your company wants to move to a cloud provider to be able to scale resources quickly, but it is concerned about the security of confidential information. Which of the following types of cloud models might be the most appropriate for your company?\
A- public\
B- private\
C- community \
D- hybrid\
\
*D. A hybrid cloud provides the best of public and private clouds. You get the scalability and cost effectiveness of a public cloud but also the security that you need for important files on the private portion of the cloud.\
\
4-You have been asked to advise a group of several universities that want to combine research efforts and store data in the cloud. Which type of cloud solution might be best for them?\
A- public\
B- private\
C- community\
D- hybrid\
\
*C. When multiple organizations with similar objectives want to combine efforts in a cloud, the best choice is generally a community cloud. This allows for the flexibility and scalability normally found in a public cloud, but it also limits the number of users to a smaller, trusted group. Hybrid clouds also combine public and private, but are for a single company to use.\
\
5- Your manager wants to use the cloud because everyone seems to be talking about it. What should you include when you are listing the benefits of using the cloud? (Choose all that apply)\
A- increased security\
B- increased scalability\
C- lower cost\
D- improved reliability\
\
*B,C,D. Cloud solutions are great for enhancing scalability and reliability while generally lowering costs. Security could be an issue with cloud computing, depending on your organization\'92s needs, because the resources aren\'92t locally controlled and managed\
\
6- You have been asked to configure a client-side virtualization solution with three guest OSs. Each one needs Internet access. How should you configure the solution I the most cost effective way?\
A- three physical NICs\
B- one physical NICs, three virtual NICs, and one virtual switch\
C- one physical NICs, one virtual NIC, and three virtual switches\
D- one physical NICs, three virtual NICs, and three virtual switches\
\
*B. Each virtual machine will use its own virtual NIC, so you need three virtual NICs. The virtual NICs will communicate with one virtual switch managed by the hypervisor. The virtual switch will communicate with one physical NIC on the host system.\
\
7- You have been asked to install Linux in a VM on a Windows 11 client. The Windows 11 client needs 4 GB of RAM, and Linux needs 2 GB of RAM. How much RAM does the system  need at a minimum?\
A- 4GB\
B- 6 GB\
C- 8 GB\
D- unable to determine from the questions\
\
*B. There needs to be enough RAM to support both OSs, so the answer is 6 GB. More is better, though!\
\
8- A computer using which of the following would be considered a legacy device? (Choose all that apply)\
A- a 386 processor\
B- the IPX/SPX protocol\
C- an application \
D- 1 GB of RAM\
\
*A, B, C. Legacy systems are the ones that use older hardware, software or network protocols that are not commonly used today. A system with only 1 GB of RAM might be woefully underpowered, but that in and of itself does not make it a legacy system.\
\
9- you have been asked to set up client-side virtualization on an office computer. The host OS is Windows 11, and there will be three Windows 11 guest OSs. Which of the following is true about the need for antivirus security?\
A- the host OS needs an antivirus program, but virtual machines can\'92t be affected by viruses.\
B- the host OS antivirus software will also protect the guest OSs on the VMs\
C- installing antivirus software on the virtual switch will protect all guests OSs\
D- the host OS and each guest OS need their own antivirus software installed\
\
*D. Each instance of the OS you are running requires its own security software.\
\
10. You need to set up a temporary operating system environment to quickly test a piece of software your manager wants to install on the network. Which should you use?\
A- AAA server\
B- Sandbox\
C- SCADA\
D- application virtualization\
\
*B. A sandbox is a temporary operating system environment, kind of like a lite version of a virtual machine. It\'92s ideal for testing software such as this. An AAA server is for authentication, authorization, and accounting of security. Supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) is a hardware and/or software environment used to control industrial systems, and in many cases it is older, so therefore it is considered legacy. Application virtualization is used for legacy apps or cross-platform virtualization. \
\
\
11. You have been asked to setup client-side virtualization on a computer at work. The manager asks for a type 2 hypervisor. What is the disadvantage of using that type of hypervisor?\
A- the guest OS will compete for resources with the host OS.\
B- the guest OS will be forced to a lower priority with the CPU that the host OS\
C- the guest OS will be forced to use less RAM than the host OS\
D- the virtual guest OS will not be able to get on the physical network.\
\
*A. A type 2 hypervisor sits on top of an exisiting OS, meaning that OSs installed in VMs will complete for resources with the host OS. The amount of resources available to a guest OS can be configured. Virtual OSs can get on the physical network if configured properly. \
\
12. Your software development team has created an app that needs to be quickly deployed to all network users, using virtualization. Which technology is best suited for this purpose?\
A- type 1 hypervisor\
B- type 2 hypervisor\
C- containers\
D- VDI\
\
*C. Containers are used to quickly deploy single apps and all of the files needed to run them, regardless of what platform (OS) the user is using. Hypervisors virtualize entire machines. VDI is the virtual desktop infrastructure.\
\
13- Which type of cloud is generally most cost effective for companies to use?\
A-private\
B- public\
C- hybrid\
D- community\
\
*B. Public clouds are usually the most cost effective. The client doesn\'92t need to purchase any hardware, the cloud provider benefits from economic of scale\
\
14- a development team is creating containers. Which of the following statements are not true regarding containers? (Choose two)\
A- containers are faster to deploy than hypervisors\
B- each container has a minimum RAM requirement\
C- containers can hold more than one app\
D- containers are designed to work on one OS\
\
*B,D. Containers are faster to deploy than hypervisors. They can hold more than one app, but best practices usually specify that they hold only one. Containers do not have their own RAM requirements. They are designed to work on any OS.\
\
15- Your manager read that multiple client companies might share the same hardware in a cloud and is extremely concerned about the security of company data. What should you tell them?\
A- data security is a serious concern in a multi tenancy environment, so the data should be limited to non-sensitive materials\
B- thanks to the use of containers, data from different companies always separated to help avoid data security issues\
C- cloud providers guarantee that clients will not share the same storage devices, so data security is not a significant issue\
D- multiple tenants may share the same hardware, but their data and apps are separated to avoid data security issues.\
\
*D. Multitenancy happens all the time in cloud computing, meaning that multiple clients will share the same hardware resources. Their apps and data are separated though to avoid any data security issues.\
\
16- A software developer wants to be able to test their in-progress apps in three different OSs. Which type of setup is best for their Windows 11 client computer?\
A- type 1 hypervisor \
B- type 2 hypervisor \
C- containers\
D- VDI\
\
*B. A type 2 hypervisor is the best choice. It can sit on top of the developer\'92s Windows workstation, and virtualize other OSs as needed for testing. A Type 1 (bare-metal) hypervisor is better suited for server virtualization. Containers may be useful in quick deploying the apps once they are complete and ensuring they can run in multiple operating environments. VDI is the virtual desktop infrastructure.\
\
17- A manager is demanding more storage space for his department, immediately. What type of cloud solution is best in this case?\
A- IaaS\
B- SaaS\
C- PaaS\
D- VDI\
\
*A. Infrastructure as a service (IaaS) provides hardware, which includes storage space. Platform as a service (PaaS) would include software development tools, and Software as a service (SaaS) would include apps as well. Neither of those seem needed in this instance. VDI is virtual desktop infrastructure.\
\
18-A cloud provider is asking if you know what all of the software and hardware is that\'92s needed to create an appropriate virtual environment for your users. What are they referring to?\
A- type 1 hypervisor\
B- type 2 hypervisor\
C- container\
D- VDI\
\
*D.  The virtual desktop infrastructure (vdi) is the hardware and software needed to create a virtual environment. Hypervisors are the software packages that create and manage virtual environments. Containers are used for software virtualization.\
\
19- On the latest invoice from your CSP, you notice an egress surcharge. What is this most likely for?\
A- downloading data from the cloud\
B- uploading data to the cloud\
C- creating new containers for applications\
D- creating new virtual desktop infrastructure (VDI) instances\
\
*A. Ingress ( uploading data) and egress (downloading data) may be part of metered utilization in a cloud agreement. Generally, ingress is free, but many cloud providers will charge for data egress. Egress is not related to containers or VDI.\
\
20- a CSP is setting up services for three client companies. Each client has contracted for 10 TB storage space. How much storage space does the cloud provider need to have, in total, to satisfy the contracts?\
A- 10 TB, because clients will share hardware in a multitenancy environment\
B- 20 TB, because clients will share hardware in a multi tenancy environment\
C- 30 TB, because that is what the clients contracted in total\
D- 60 TB, because the CSP must have reserve storage space in reserve for elasticity. \
\
*C. If the CSP has guaranteed three clients 10 TB each, then the CSP needs at least 30 TB of available storage space. Clients may share hardware in a multi tenancy environment, but each is guaranteed its contract terms. Having extra storage available for elasticity purposes is a good idea but not required.\
\
